                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "710e8cf4-445c-461e-a3de-e173dc0b9648",
                                "sense_id": "fa9fa648-b383-3489-a719-2142f6f861ef",
                                "text": "Allografts vascularize and are eventually rejected at which time they must be replaced. Xenografts (porcine) - not as good as homografts; last 2 weeks; these do not vascularize. Dermal substitutes - not as good as homografts or xenografts[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fb8948b1-1d0b-448f-847e-4fbae295a542",
                                "sense_id": "fa9fa648-b383-3489-a719-2142f6f861ef",
                                "text": "Despite concerted efforts, the skin substitutes available today all fail to vascularize and also there are no epidermal/dermal skin substitutes available that can close wounds permanently."
                            }
                        ]
